+<a name="feature-summary"></a>
+<h3>Search Feature Summary</h3>
+<p>
+  The following table summarizes common search syntax features. See the linked sections for full rules and examples.
+</p>
+<table class="grid">
+  <tr>
+    <td><b>Feature</b></td>
+    <td><b>Syntax</b></td>
+    <td><b>Meaning</b></td>
+  </tr>
+  <tr>
+    <td><a href="#multivalue">AND</a></td>
+    <td>Repeat the search parameter name, separated by <code>&amp;</code></td>
+    <td>Intersect results that match each supplied parameter value, such as <code>Patient?given=A&amp;given=B</code>.</td>
+  </tr>
+  <tr>
+    <td><a href="#multivalue">OR</a></td>
+    <td>Separate values with <code>,</code></td>
+    <td>Union results that match any supplied value, such as <code>Patient?given=A,B</code>.</td>
+  </tr>
+  <tr>
+    <td><a href="#modifiers">Modifiers</a></td>
+    <td>Append <code>:[modifier]</code> to the parameter name</td>
+    <td>Change the test performed by a search parameter, such as <code>Patient?given:exact=A</code>.</td>
+  </tr>
+  <tr>
+    <td><a href="#modifiertype">Reference type qualification</a></td>
+    <td>Append a concrete resource type to a reference parameter, using modifier syntax</td>
+    <td>Restrict a reference search to a target resource type, such as <code>Observation?subject:Patient=123</code>.</td>
+  </tr>
+  <tr>
+    <td><a href="#prefix">Prefixes</a></td>
+    <td>Prefix a value with codes such as <code>lt</code>, <code>ge</code>, or <code>ap</code></td>
+    <td>Change matching for ordered values, such as <code>Observation?date=ge2020</code>.</td>
+  </tr>
+  <tr>
+    <td><a href="#chaining">Chaining</a></td>
+    <td>Join reference search parameters with <code>.</code></td>
+    <td>Search through a referenced resource, such as <code>Observation?subject.name=Smith</code>.</td>
+  </tr>
+  <tr>
+    <td><a href="#escaping">Escaping</a></td>
+    <td>Escape literal <code>$</code>, <code>,</code>, <code>|</code>, and <code>\</code> characters by prepending <code>\</code></td>
+    <td>Use reserved search characters in values when they are not intended as syntax.</td>
+  </tr>
+</table>
+
